# 1. GMAIL SMTP (Primary: Sends real OTP from your Gmail via Nodemailer)
# To generate an App Password:
#   a. Ensure 2-Step Verification is enabled on your Google Account: https://myaccount.google.com/security
#   b. Go to App Passwords: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   c. Enter "Money Control" as the App Name, click Create.
#   d. Copy the 16-character code (spaces are ignored automatically).
GMAIL_USER=skaviraj416@gmail.com
GMAIL_APP_PASS=dqan kufp byaa jwwq

# 2. VERCEL / PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# If deploying to Vercel (for mobile & desktop access):
# In your Vercel Project Dashboard:
#   Settings -> Environment Variables -> Add:
#     - Key: GMAIL_USER, Value: skaviraj416@gmail.com
#     - Key: GMAIL_APP_PASS, Value: dqan kufp byaa jwwq
#   Select Environments: Production, Preview, Development.
#   Click Save, then Redeploy.

# 3. OPTIONAL FRONTEND API BASE URL
# By default, frontend calls relative '/api/send-otp' which resolves to the current origin.
# If hosting frontend and backend on different domains or testing in hybrid wrappers:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://money-control-beta-one.vercel.app

# 4. Alternative Cloud Email Providers (Optional fallbacks)
